{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/yang-clojure/1794735000000-engineer-d1-r12-declaration-completion.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md'","aggregated_output":"# D1 r12 — claim and phase preflight, in progress\n\nWorktree mirror; no commit. No complete declaration, bounded corpus verification, D1 companion or verification result exists. The r9e store at `target/d1-r9e-retained-store` stays uncommitted; retention location and ownership remain pending.\n\nThe first complete upstream symbol/arity query plan (`1794735000000-engineer-d1-r12-claim-plan.edn`) contains 165 admitted symbol/arity claims, 23 with supplied carrier paths. It is explicitly marked producer-derived and not independently verified: the input carrier relation is the oracle harness's own `kernel-ambient-correspondence`. `yang.correspondence-claims/claim-plan!` validates scoping, supported carrier modes, duplicate inventory and deterministic order; these checks do not establish the truth of the supplied relation. This is a pilot claim plan, not a verifier result.\n\n`verify-retained-fixture!` records separate row-fetch, direct-content-fetch, replay and gate elapsed times; the gate records tree-check, independent static check, mutated-declaration check and scoped query elapsed times, with per-lane run times. Red-first tests exercise both phase maps. The pre-declaration full-claim pilot `target/d1-r12-claim-phase-pilot.clj` runs against all r9e outcomes using the 165 supplied claims and produces `1794735000000-engineer-d1-r12-claim-phase-pilot.edn`. It is a pilot, not a bounded verification run, and every final outcome is labeled `:pre-declaration true`. The initial store open was 195,419 ms, measured separately. Progress is per fixture and includes refusals or candidate-limit failures; consult the file for the current outcome counts. Its limits are pilot safety caps, not a declared run.\n\nThe r11 69,936 ms full-path datum and the 62,949 ms inner-gate datum remain the evidence that the earlier 60,000 ms non-binding candidate has insufficient headroom. The full-claim pilot adds phase and workload samples but does not independently validate carrier paths or establish the true B/S C1/provenance baseline, complete retained recipe and derivation chain, process-level failure supervision, a full declaration or a verification publication. No previously declared ceiling was raised; none was frozen. Do not present a pilot pass as D1 verification or use its producer-supplied carrier relation as independent reconstruction.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
