{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > collab/yang-clojure/1794735000000-engineer-d1-r12-declaration-completion.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md <<'EOF'\n# D1 r12 — measured claim pilot and independent carrier preflight\n\nWorktree mirror; no commit. The complete declaration, bounded corpus verification, D1 companion and verification result remain unfinished. The r9e store \"'`target/d1-r9e-retained-store` remains uncommitted; its retention location and ownership remain an OWNER DECISION.\n\n## Claim inventory and independent carrier check\n\nThe initial claim plan (`1794735000000-engineer-d1-r12-claim-plan.edn`) contains 165 admitted symbol/arity claims and 23 carrier relationships. It was derived using the oracle harness'\"'s carrier relation and marked as producer-derived. A separate implementation, \"'`yang.correspondence-claims/derive-carriers!`, independently derives the carrier relationships from the source forms, supplied adaptation configuration and explicit symbol resolution map, and refuses missing resolutions. Its result (`1794735000000-engineer-d1-r12-carrier-check.edn`) agrees for all 23 relationships; the independently reconstructed 165-claim plan is `1794735000000-engineer-d1-r12-independent-claim-plan.edn`. This is an independent derivation implementation, but it uses the same supplied source/environment inputs; their full executable closure is not yet retained and independently verified. Agreement is not a D1 verification result.\n\n## Pre-declaration fixture pilot\n\n`verify-retained-fixture!` now records row-fetch, direct-content-fetch, replay and gate elapsed times; the gate records tree, independent static, mutation and query phases. `1794735000000-engineer-d1-r12-claim-phase-pilot.edn` records all 155 r9e fixtures passing the existing gate with 165 supplied queries and both guarded lanes. Each outcome is labeled `:pre-declaration true`; these pilot passes do not certify D1. The initial store open took 195,419 ms, separately. Maximum fixture time was 67,358 ms, with a 5 ms sampled process used-heap peak of 3,880,862,784 bytes. The draft records phase maxima and comparability limits. The r11 69,936 ms datum remains the larger full-fixture observation from the handoff; the previous 60,000 ms candidate was never frozen and is inadequate. No declaration ceiling was raised.\n\nThe per-fixture pilot maxima included 2,544,482 walker and 1,398,649 semantic instructions; each lane reached up to 2,345 records and 67,500 printed bytes. The pilot records outcomes incrementally. A pass means this gate completed, not that every upstream claim was credited or all D1 obligations were verified.\n\n## Static C1 comparison preflight\n\n`yang.correspondence-static/compare-static!` materializes the same retained tree in separate in-memory baseline and C1 stores, reconstructs and checks call-site markers from application occurrences, and times publication, load and a relation query. It is an exploratory static comparison: it does not reconstruct the compiler/recipe or complete provenance, does not run a guest, does not publish the relation as an index, and repeated calls in one JVM are not independent cold starts. Its progress file is `1794735000000-engineer-d1-r12-static-c1-pilot.edn`; it is not a declaration or verification result.\n\n## Required continuation\n\nComplete actual B/S/T comparisons, including end-to-end provenance production and required phase/memory measurements, and retain the independent recipe, image, derivation and instruction provenance closure. Integrate live enforcement for every declared quantity and process-level timeout/memory failure supervision so a failed fixture cannot terminate the corpus. Freeze a complete measured, finite, max-based laptop declaration before the tagged run; then execute all 155 independently, preserving any per-fixture exceeded value and ceiling, and publish the companion and verification result based on the retained admissions. The current partial gate checks elapsed time at phase boundaries and sampled used heap; those do not enforce hard process time or heap ceilings. The executable recipe remains a concrete r13 gap. Never substitute the pilot or a producer claim for the verifier'\"'s missing evidence.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
